      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The slow river
    number: 8
    heartsNeeded: 8
    path: 0
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I have a ticket. For the spring. I have not told anyone. Now I have told you.
    - Walt will be angry. Gus will be rude. Yuki will be... I do not know what Yuki will be. That is what frightens me.
    - Should I simply go, and write to her from the boat, where it is easier? Or tell her first, face to face, and let her decide some of it with me?
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 1
      optionA: Go home
      replyA:
      - Then I will go. The slow river reaches the sea too.
      - I will tell her this week. Before I lose my nerve. And then I will tell Walt, who will need a chair.
      flagsA:
      - kenji_going_home
      optionB: Tell Yuki first
      replyB:
      - Face to face. Yes. You are right, though I wish you were not.
      - Tonight, at dinner. I will make her favourite. That way, if it goes badly, at least the food will be good.
      flagsB:
      - kenji_told_yuki
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: The farewell
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - The street gave me a party in the plaza. Rosa made a cake shaped like a chessboard. Mi-sook made enough food for the whole of Japan.
    - Walt cried. He says it was the pollen. Gus said, 'You'll be back,' and then he hugged me so hard my glasses came off.
    - Yuki has promised to visit every summer. The crow was on the roof of the general store the whole evening. Watching. I think he knows.
    happy: 0
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Yuki's answer
    number: 9
    heartsNeeded: 9
    path: 2
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - I told her. She was quiet for a long time. Then she went into her room and came back with a folder.
    - Inside were museum papers. Leave of absence, a whole season, already signed. She had been planning to ask ME if we could go to Japan together, to see her uncle.
    - Two people, each too frightened to say the same thing. We laughed until the tea went cold. We will go together, in spring, and come back together.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      friendship: 0
  - title: Good morning
    number: 10
    heartsNeeded: 10
    path: 1
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - A postcard came for you this morning. From Japan. Emeka brought it himself, very carefully, as if it were made of glass.
    - '''The sea is the same. My brother is slower than me at chess, which is wonderful. Please say good morning to the crow for me.'''
    - ...And when you went to the field and said it, the crow said it back. Did you hear? 'Kraa.' That is good morning, in crow. He was waiting for the right person.
    happy: 1
    ask:
      item: {fileID: 0}
      amount: 0
      minQuality: 0
      questTitle: 
      questText: 
      reminder: []
      thanks: []
    choice:
      enabled: 0
      optionA: 
      replyA: []
      flagsA: []
      optionB: 
      replyB: []
      flagsB: []
    setFlags: []
    reward:
      gold: 0
      item: {fileID: 11400000, guid: c47c97feb4e379f4382a8330972aab67, type: 2}
      amount: 3
      friendship: 0
  - title: Good morning
    number: 10
    heartsNeeded: 10
    path: 2
    conditions:
      days: 0
      seasons: 0
      dayFrom: 0
      dayTo: 0
      minYear: 0
      minTotalDays: 0
      weather: 0
      requireFlags: []
      anyFlags: []
      forbidFlags: []
      counters: []
    pages:
    - We leave in spring, and we come back in autumn. Walt has made me promise to bring him a Japanese chess set so he can lose in two languages.
    - And this morning, on the field, I said good morning to the crow as always.
    - He looked at me. He hopped closer. And he said 'Kraa.' Two years, and a bag of your corn, and he said good morning. You see? The slow river reaches the sea.
    happy: 1
